## 6. Mathematical Scoring Formulation

The Creditworthiness Signal is calculated using a **transparent, normalized multi-factor weighted sum** scaled between 0 and 100:

$$\text{Final Signal} = 0.20 \cdot S_{\text{rev\_cons}} + 0.25 \cdot S_{\text{cf\_stab}} + 0.15 \cdot S_{\text{rev\_growth}} + 0.15 \cdot S_{\text{txn\_reg}} + 0.15 \cdot S_{\text{exp\_stab}} + 0.10 \cdot S_{\text{pay\_reg}}$$

### Component Sub-Score Definitions (Each Normalized 0–100):

| Component | Weight | Metric Evaluated | Normalization Logic |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Revenue Consistency ($S_{\text{rev\_cons}}$)** | **20%** | Coefficient of Variation of monthly revenue ($CV_R$) | $100 \times \max(0, 1 - 2 \times CV_R)$ |
| **Cash-Flow Stability ($S_{\text{cf\_stab}}$)** | **25%** | Positive cash flow month ratio & net margin | $70 \times \left(\frac{\text{Pos Months}}{\text{Total Months}}\right) + 30 \times \min\left(1, \frac{\text{Net Margin}}{0.20}\right)$ |
| **Revenue Growth ($S_{\text{rev\_growth}}$)** | **15%** | Recent vs. previous period revenue growth | $50 + 2.5 \times \text{Growth \%}$ (clamped between 0 and 100) |
| **Transaction Regularity ($S_{\text{txn\_reg}}$)** | **15%** | Active days per month & absence of dormancy gaps | $100 - (\text{Max Gap Days} \times 2.5)$ (min 0) |
| **Expense Stability ($S_{\text{exp\_stab}}$)** | **15%** | Expense ratio health & count of expense spikes | $100 - (\text{Spike Count} \times 25) - \max(0, \text{Expense Ratio} - 85\%)$ |
| **Payment Regularity ($S_{\text{pay\_reg}}$)** | **10%** | Digital payment share (UPI + Bank Transfer) | $(\% \text{ UPI} + \% \text{ Bank Transfer}) \times 100$ |

